          %p
          %h2#section_Idea Idea
          %p
            The counterpart to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
            but for
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, b)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+products"} cartesian products
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+types"} product types
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
          %p
          %h2#section_Definition Definition
          %p
          %h3#section_In_set_theory In set theory
          %p
            Product extensionality states that for all elements
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a' \in A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b' \in B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = a'
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = b'
            if and only if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, b) = (a', b')
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
            to make the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairing+structure"} pairing structure
            into an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+pairing+structure"} ordered pairing structure
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, b)
          %p
          %h3#section_In_type_theory In type theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            is represented by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
          %p
            Instead, product extensionality is the statement that given types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+function+application+to+identities"} binary function application to identities
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} apbinary
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{apbinary}_{(-,-)}(a, a', b, b')
            of the function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A, b:B \vdash (a, b):A \times B
            defined in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/introduction+rule"} introduction rule
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+type"} product type
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
            for all elements
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a':A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:A
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b':A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prodext
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
